1. A computer-implemented method for smart lighting control executed by a user device (100), the method comprising:

capturing, via a camera (102) of the user device (100), an image of a physical environment illuminated by a smart lighting device (300), wherein the captured image includes a distorted projected light pattern (204) cast onto a physical surface (200) within the physical environment, the distorted projected light pattern (204) comprising a plurality of embedded marker sources (206);

detecting, by one or more processors (104) of the user device (100), the plurality of embedded marker sources (206) within the distorted projected light pattern (204);

calculating, by the one or more processors (104), a geometric transformation based on a spatial distortion of the detected plurality of embedded marker sources (206) relative to an expected geometric arrangement of marker sources;

aligning, by the one or more processors (104), an interactive user interface (UI) control overlay (208) with the physical surface (200) on a display (106) of the user device (100) using the calculated geometric transformation;

receiving, via the aligned interactive UI control overlay (208) rendered on the display (106), a user input specifying at least one lighting parameter adjustment; and

transmitting, via a wireless communication interface (108) of the user device (100), a control command corresponding to the specified lighting parameter adjustment to the smart lighting device (300) to modify a light output of the smart lighting device (300).
